3. Monte Carlo Uncertainty Propagation Code
The Monte Carlo code (mc_uncertainty.py) propagates the five uncertainty sources (Eₐ, wall thickness, emissivity, ambient temperature, inspection time) through the lumped ODE solution (Equation 5) to compute detection probability.

python
import numpy as np
from scipy.stats import norm, uniform

def sample_uncertainties(n_samples):
    # E_a: coefficient of variation 15% around nominal 1.5 MJ
    E_a = norm.rvs(loc=1.5, scale=0.15*1.5, size=n_samples)
    # wall thickness: uniform ±1 mm around 15 mm
    thick = uniform.rvs(loc=14e-3, scale=2e-3, size=n_samples)
    # emissivity: uniform ±0.02 around 0.12
    eps = uniform.rvs(loc=0.10, scale=0.04, size=n_samples)
    # ambient temperature: normal ±3°C around 25°C
    T_amb = norm.rvs(loc=25, scale=3, size=n_samples)
    # inspection time: uniform ±2 min around 10 min
    t_insp = uniform.rvs(loc=8*60, scale=4*60, size=n_samples)  # seconds
